    <!-- Privacy page -->
    <string name="privacy_title">Privacy</string>
    <string name="privacy_body">RabbitAV runs entirely on your phone.\n\nStored on device:\n• Hazard sites (type, location, confidence, timestamps)\n• Trips (route stats, alert counts — no video)\n• Mount calibration profiles\n• A rolling in-memory log for diagnostics\n\nNever stored, never uploaded:\n• Camera video or images (frames are processed live and discarded)\n• Audio\n\nIf you enable anonymous sync, only hazard events (type, coordinates, heading, speed, confidence, timestamp) plus a random resettable device ID are uploaded. Imagery never leaves the device.</string>

    <!-- OEM guidance -->
    <string name="oem_title">Keep RabbitAV alive</string>
    <string name="oem_intro">Many Android brands aggressively kill background apps, which would end a drive session mid-highway. Apply the steps for your brand:</string>
    <string name="oem_xiaomi">Xiaomi / MIUI · Settings → Apps → Manage apps → RabbitAV → Autostart ON; Battery saver → No restrictions. Also lock the app in Recents (pull down on its card).</string>
    <string name="oem_vivo">Vivo / Funtouch · i Manager → App manager → Autostart manager → allow RabbitAV; Settings → Battery → High background power consumption → allow.</string>
    <string name="oem_oppo">Oppo / ColorOS · Settings → Battery → App battery management → RabbitAV → Allow background activity; Startup manager → allow autostart.</string>
    <string name="oem_realme">Realme · Settings → App management → App list → RabbitAV → Allow auto-launch; Battery → App battery management → Don\'t optimize.</string>
    <string name="oem_samsung">Samsung / One UI · Settings → Battery → Background usage limits → remove RabbitAV from Sleeping apps; add to Never sleeping apps.</string>
    <string name="oem_generic">All phones · Grant the battery-optimization exemption below and keep the app pinned in Recents during first drives.</string>

